p.src:
Unlike the free gas, the position integral does not merely yield the container volume. The restoring potential weights each displacement: $Z_{\rm cl}
 =\frac{1}{h}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}dp
             \int_{-\infty}^{\infty}dx\,
 e^{-\beta p^2/(2m)}
 e^{-\beta\kappa x^2/2}.$ The factor $1/h$ makes a one-dimensional classical partition function dimensionless. It is suppressed in the board calculation because it is independent of $\beta$ and cannot affect the mean energy.

