p.src:
When $\beta\hbar\omega\ll1$, $e^{-\beta\hbar\omega}
 =1-\beta\hbar\omega
  +O\!\left((\beta\hbar\omega)^2\right).$ The numerator of  approaches $\hbar\omega$, while the denominator is $\beta\hbar\omega$ to leading order. Therefore $E_{\rm exc}\simeq\frac{1}{\beta}=T.$ The quantum answer recovers classical equipartition when many level spacings fit inside the thermal energy.

